  "design": {
    "decision": "Sequence winners together: hold a side [A] until partner's [K] has won, give up losers early, and keep the lead once the run starts instead of cashing winners at random.",
    "opponent": "Revealed on the fourth consecutive win. Opponents break runs by ducking to win a cheap trick, or by trumping in early.",
    "rationale": "The brief asks for Streaks pieces built on four in a row. The kept pool has the four-in-a-row trigger as +mult and points but not as a ×multiplier, which is the category that scales late in a run. The earlier ub-four-row-xmult measured far below the control at ×1.5, but its amount slope was positive (+2.9 per doubling). +35 mult (the kept seed) is worth about ×3 or more early, so ×3 is the honest starting amount, not a near-duplicate retry. The fire rate is about 36–41%.",
